==Strategy==
The strategy of this stage is simple. Bring at least 3-4 meatshields, heavy hitters (Eg. Greater Balrog, Courier Cat, Can Can Cat and Dual Islands), critters (preferably spammable to ensure that you always have a critter on the field) or you can use Long Distance/Omni-Strike units that can snipe the base, and lastly sort of tanky units with fast attack rate like Ramen Cat. If you are struggling with this stage then bringing Cat Combos which raise your Worker Cat's starting level really helps by allowing you to start spamming your attackers much earlier (Eg. [[Itchy Riches (Combo)|Itchy Riches]], [[Longnecks (Combo)|Longnecks]] or [[Cat Transport (Combo)|Cat Transport]]). Cats that either resist or are immune to freeze help a lot in this stage. Lastly, Ubers will obviously help you beat this stage, but using Ubers on this stage is a bit difficult due to the low amount of money dropped by the enemies, but bringing Worker Cat starting level combos will help tremendously in Ubercarrying. Good Luck!

